{
  "about": "Which painting shows a place, by what kind of place it is (see src/ui/scenery.ts and src/ui/scene-kinds.ts). First an author's own choice for a place (places, by its id). Then what the place is, by the words of its name and of its id (kinds, the first that names it, in order; where only its level or its site names a kind, that kind, and a room's own plain kind such as a hall or a passage gives way to it): a kind's ground is how it is painted seen from the open (a green, a road, a ruin), its room how it is painted from within (a taproom, a crypt). A kind with nothing listed for how it is seen shows no painting, only a dim ground: a dark room is better than a cathedral for a taproom (the owner, 7 November). Otherwise a settlement by its land, wild country by its land or its region's terrain, a site, the night; the way into a town at a new game's opening (approaches); under a roof and under the ground with no kind (within). Each kind has a few, and a place is given the same one each time. Chosen by looking at the paintings (seen.json): never a sight the place's words deny, never a figure who could be taken for someone met. Winter paintings are shown only in winter. Add a painting's name to a list to use it; nothing in the engine needs to change. What is still wanted is in doc/paintings/commission-list.md.",
